{"availability":"available","full":"vaishsRP/Bol-Sustainability-Layer","name":"Bol-Sustainability-Layer","description":"Sustainability scoring layer for bol.com products, built at a hackathon. Python scoring pipeline plus a Next.js storefront demo.","category":"Business","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-08-03T16:11:25Z","updated":"2026-08-03T17:33:55Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://bol-com-solution.vercel.app/","topics":["ecommerce","greenwashing","hackathon","nextjs","python","sustainability","typescript"],"demo":"https://bol-com-solution.vercel.app/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T02:58:39.953Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-17T02:58:39.953Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-17T02:58:39.953Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T18:23:22.885Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-11T06:11:15.600Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-17T02:58:39.953Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Next.js","Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Hackathon project for the bol.com sustainability case, June 2026. Team Ctrl+V, two people. We called it The Honest Price Tag.","live demo: ps: it runs on a free vercel account so it may be slow to wake up.","The case gave us a catalog of 1,000 products where the sustainability fields are half empty and sometimes contradict each other. The example that shaped the whole project: a phone speaker in the set carries a Cradle to Cradle certificate, and the data under that certificate shows plastic packaging, shipping from Japan, and 168 kg of CO2 to manufacture. The certificate is real. The product is still a bad pick. We built a layer that scores what the data says instead of what the label claims."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/vaishsRP/Bol-Sustainability-Layer/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"d0abe05d727a28a8e1c142142e829068e94609c9ccdaf2a759fb8328713a4ca7","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T18:23:23.017Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T18:23:23.017Z","p